  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance and Hygiene Services to IDPs, Refugees</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seven months after fighting erupted, Sudan is facing one of the fastest unfolding crises globally, with unprecedented needs in such a short period. Close to 6.2 million people &#x2013; about one in every eight people in the country - have fled their homes since the conflict between the Sudanese Armed Forces (SAF) and the Rapid Support Forces (RSF) started in mid-April. To respond to some of the immediate needs of IDPs, Refugees, and host communities in Sudan, in close consultation with the Bishops of Sudan, CAFOD, CRS and Caritas Sudan coordinated with the CI secretariat in Rome and agreed to launch the appeal. 
 
This appeal seeks to secure continued support for the IDPs, refugees, and host communities in White Nile. The lead agency for implementation of the Appeal is Caritas Sudan and remains supported by CAFOD (see section eight), to maintain strategic oversight and coordination of the response.</narrative>
  </description>
